WEBVTT

00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:44.043
FLEX X COP 2

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:46.837
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:48.966
ALL CHILD ACTORS FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:00.227
Joo.

00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:02.813
Would you like something to drink?

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:05.941
You did a great job.

00:01:06.525 --> 00:01:08.193
You too, sir.

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:13.948
Working with you again felt like old times.

00:01:13.949 --> 00:01:16.033
I could really count on you.

00:01:16.034 --> 00:01:17.119
Me too.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.122
What did you think of Jin Isoo?

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:24.042
He can be a bit odd,

00:01:25.127 --> 00:01:26.712
And he's unpredictable,

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.672
But he's got good instincts.

00:01:29.673 --> 00:01:31.383
And he's quite serious about the job.

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:33.217
Right?

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:36.013
He's actually a decent detective.

00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:39.725
Do you have someone lined up to lead Team 1?

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:45.147
No.

00:01:46.023 --> 00:01:47.024
No one.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.863
So I was wondering...

00:01:53.905 --> 00:01:56.199
Someone just like you would be perfect for the job.

00:01:57.284 --> 00:01:58.659
Someone who's capable,

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.580
Can manage Detective Jin, and has real charisma.

00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:05.667
Someone of that caliber

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:08.003
Is really hard to come by.

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:15.760
Hello!

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.724
When did you have time to make these?

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:23.727
Hi there! Want a photo?

00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:27.396
He's going overboard again.

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:29.273
Come on, it's all good fun.

00:02:29.274 --> 00:02:30.608
Okay, band.

00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:31.776
Let's give it a try.

00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:33.445
Just like we practiced. Ready!

00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:47.708
-  Stop! -  What in the world...

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:49.920
What is all this?

00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:51.713
Sir!

00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:54.924
Oh, for heaven's sake.

00:02:54.925 --> 00:02:57.219
- That good for nothing... - Sir.

00:02:57.803 --> 00:03:00.097
Come on, clear all this out.

00:03:00.639 --> 00:03:02.723
- This was Jin Isoo's doing. - Sir!

00:03:02.724 --> 00:03:04.892
It's for my new boss. You know the drill.

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:05.894
Let's do this.

00:03:08.772 --> 00:03:10.231
Somebody's working hard.

00:03:10.232 --> 00:03:12.817
Of course. We're getting a new team leader.

00:03:12.818 --> 00:03:13.944
Of course.

00:03:15.362 --> 00:03:17.363
Oh. Incoming!

00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:43.181
Joo Hyera?

00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:02.491
I didn't expect such a grand welcome.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:07.038
Detective Jin has been busy since this morning.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.708
I guess you can be sweet.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:13.628
This is the new team leader of Violent Crime Investigation Team 1, Joo Hyera. :cue

00:04:15.005 --> 00:04:16.548
She's got years on you boys.

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:20.301
She was on our Violent Crime Team before moving to Counterterrorism.

00:04:21.386 --> 00:04:24.514
Detective Jin, take good care of your new boss.

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:27.392
Take good care of her.

00:04:32.522 --> 00:04:33.732
Detective Jin Isoo,

00:04:34.566 --> 00:04:37.276
Detective Park Junyoung, Detective Choi Kyungjin.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.653
Glad to join the team.

00:04:40.697 --> 00:04:42.281
This has to be a nightmare.

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:43.325
It's real.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.410
Get used to it.

00:04:54.377 --> 00:04:55.754
Looking forward to it, nutjob.

00:05:06.765 --> 00:05:07.766
But why?

00:05:09.643 --> 00:05:12.812
She has it good in Counterterrorism, so why, huh?

00:05:12.813 --> 00:05:14.021
That's true.

00:05:14.022 --> 00:05:15.606
Why the sudden transfer?

00:05:15.607 --> 00:05:17.817
I'm seriously doomed.

00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:19.777
What are you talking about?

00:05:19.778 --> 00:05:21.947
She's a capable, experienced veteran detective.

00:05:22.823 --> 00:05:24.406
We don't get along.

00:05:24.407 --> 00:05:25.951
She doesn't like me.

00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:29.913
Nutjob. Hey, nutjob.

00:05:31.665 --> 00:05:32.748
Hey, nutjob!

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.627
Hey, nutjob!

00:05:36.628 --> 00:05:37.879
Hey, nutjob.

00:05:44.553 --> 00:05:45.719
It's nothing new.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.429
I didn't like you at first, either.

00:05:50.809 --> 00:05:51.976
Sir!

00:05:51.977 --> 00:05:53.435
What?

00:05:53.436 --> 00:05:54.812
So...

00:05:54.813 --> 00:05:56.939
About Detective Joo Hyera.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.400
I heard she worked here before.

00:05:58.984 --> 00:06:00.192
Yeah.

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:02.611
We worked together for about a year or so.

00:06:02.612 --> 00:06:06.115
Then why did she come back here?

00:06:06.116 --> 00:06:07.117
Beats me.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.411
Ah.

00:06:09.911 --> 00:06:11.203
It must be to torment you.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.707
Come on, be serious!

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:15.584
She's good at her job.

00:06:16.251 --> 00:06:18.127
She's pretty laid-back, so don't worry.

00:06:19.921 --> 00:06:21.005
How old is she?

00:06:22.674 --> 00:06:24.049
Same age as you, I think.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.468
- Same age as me? - Yes.

00:06:28.138 --> 00:06:31.683
By the way, don't ever make bets with her.

00:06:32.267 --> 00:06:34.935
- Why not? - She's kind of competitive...

00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:37.188
No, she's insanely competitive.

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.065
She always has to win.

00:06:44.821 --> 00:06:46.323
Hmm...

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:57.959
Yes, come in.

00:07:00.295 --> 00:07:02.797
Oh, Detective Joo Hyera. Come in and have a seat.

00:07:08.011 --> 00:07:10.095
I appreciate you taking on this tough role.

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.347
Not at all.

00:07:11.348 --> 00:07:14.099
You also successfully closed the bombing case.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.435
We're lucky to have you.

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:17.312
You're too kind.

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:21.983
By the way, I have one favor to ask of you.

00:07:22.651 --> 00:07:23.985
Of course. Please, go ahead.

00:07:24.569 --> 00:07:26.237
It's about Jin Isoo.

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:30.658
I can't sleep at night because of him.

00:07:30.659 --> 00:07:32.409
Strictly speaking,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:36.539
Those bombings wouldn't have happened if it weren't for him.

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:40.959
What's a spoiled rich kid doing running wild in the police force?

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:44.881
God knows what he did, but he won over everyone in Violent Crime and Chief Park.

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:48.093
Discipline's gone to hell around here.

00:07:49.052 --> 00:07:51.805
Discipline's important in an organization.

00:07:53.181 --> 00:07:54.182
Which is why

00:07:54.808 --> 00:07:57.894
You should watch him, and when he's about to cause trouble,

00:07:58.687 --> 00:08:01.106
Report it to me. I'll use it to kick him out.

00:08:02.524 --> 00:08:03.607
Yes, sir.

00:08:03.608 --> 00:08:05.985
Good. I'm counting on you.

00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:08.570
I also have a favor to ask.

00:08:08.571 --> 00:08:10.155
Yes, what is it?

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:11.824
Once Jin Isoo leaves,

00:08:11.825 --> 00:08:13.368
I'd like to pick his replacement.

00:08:14.119 --> 00:08:15.619
Sure, you do that.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:16.621
Yes, sir. :cue

00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:34.848
Detective Jin.

00:08:36.266 --> 00:08:37.267
Got something to say?

00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:39.686
Nope.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.563
We can finish the report tomorrow.

00:08:42.564 --> 00:08:43.647
Let's go out for drinks tonight.

00:08:43.648 --> 00:08:44.649
Okay.

00:08:45.692 --> 00:08:47.901
Then I know this celebrity chef...

00:08:47.902 --> 00:08:50.070
Let's go somewhere local, in one hour.

00:08:50.071 --> 00:08:51.489
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:56.286 --> 00:08:59.289
She's the worst. Seriously, the worst.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.332
The absolute worst.

00:09:10.216 --> 00:09:11.843
Okay, let's make a toast.

00:09:16.681 --> 00:09:17.724
Bro.

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:23.437
- Here's to working together. - Welcome to the team!

00:09:23.438 --> 00:09:25.440
- Welcome. -  Welcome.

00:09:34.032 --> 00:09:36.825
Chief Park? He was my immediate supervisor.

00:09:36.826 --> 00:09:38.703
Wow! What was he like?

00:09:39.287 --> 00:09:40.747
He was scary.

00:09:41.873 --> 00:09:43.165
I learned a lot from him.

00:09:43.166 --> 00:09:44.583
We heard so much about you.

00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:46.585
- Like how you caught Kim Dusik. - Kim Dusik?

00:09:46.586 --> 00:09:48.504
Yeah, a serial robber and killer.

00:09:48.505 --> 00:09:50.380
I heard you spent a week on stakeout.

00:09:50.381 --> 00:09:52.216
People still talk about that?

00:09:52.217 --> 00:09:53.509
Of course.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.511
A whole week? Where?

00:09:55.637 --> 00:09:58.597
The convenience store in front of his girlfriend's house.

00:09:58.598 --> 00:09:59.765
I worked there.

00:09:59.766 --> 00:10:02.267
I caught him when he came to buy cigarettes at dawn.

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:05.021
But...

00:10:05.814 --> 00:10:08.399
...why did you come back?

00:10:10.693 --> 00:10:11.861
That's...

00:10:13.238 --> 00:10:14.489
No comment.

00:10:15.448 --> 00:10:16.658
"No comment," my foot.

00:10:18.952 --> 00:10:20.787
- Bro, where are you going? -  The restroom.

00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:24.081
Then, tell us about the chief.

00:10:24.082 --> 00:10:25.083
The chief?

00:10:25.917 --> 00:10:27.167
What kind of stuff?

00:10:27.168 --> 00:10:29.336
Something cool, or something dirty?

00:10:29.337 --> 00:10:30.420
Something dirty.

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:34.258
It was summer, around five years ago.

00:10:34.259 --> 00:10:35.676
It was a scorching hot day.

00:10:35.677 --> 00:10:37.427
It turns out that bastard

00:10:37.428 --> 00:10:39.556
Was hiding in a pigsty.

00:10:40.223 --> 00:10:42.349
The chief just dove right in.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.934
No way.

00:10:43.935 --> 00:10:45.269
The chief?

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.771
The stench was unbearable, but we couldn't say a word.

00:10:47.772 --> 00:10:50.941
His wife told him at the door to strip down and throw it all away.

00:10:54.404 --> 00:10:56.030
I didn't expect that from him.

00:10:56.906 --> 00:10:58.073
We didn't order these.

00:10:58.074 --> 00:10:59.993
Ah. Over there.

00:11:04.372 --> 00:11:05.873
No way!

00:11:05.874 --> 00:11:07.333
SCORE OVER 1,000 FOR 4 FREE BEERS

00:11:08.293 --> 00:11:10.003
Isoo scored over 1,000 points.

00:11:15.717 --> 00:11:18.760
This isn't something just anyone can do.

00:11:18.761 --> 00:11:20.013
"Just anyone?"

00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:23.056
You haven't seen the champion's photo yet?

00:11:23.057 --> 00:11:24.058
Champion?

00:11:27.478 --> 00:11:28.479
DART CHAMPION

00:11:29.272 --> 00:11:30.689
- Ooh. - That's amazing.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.984
Champion?

00:11:34.485 --> 00:11:36.738
I'm taking that champion's place today.

00:11:38.615 --> 00:11:39.781
- Ooh. - Oh!

00:11:39.782 --> 00:11:41.825
Great shot!

00:11:41.826 --> 00:11:42.827
Talk is cheap.

00:11:52.295 --> 00:11:54.047
So cool. :cue

00:12:20.156 --> 00:12:21.783
Please could you stop them?

00:12:22.951 --> 00:12:23.952
We're sorry.

00:12:28.831 --> 00:12:30.457
You stepped on the line.

00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:31.875
Okay, fine.

00:12:31.876 --> 00:12:33.752
I thought he said they don't get along.

00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:35.046
They get along really well.

00:12:37.423 --> 00:12:38.632
Oh!

00:12:38.633 --> 00:12:40.467
Detective Joo won.

00:12:40.468 --> 00:12:42.803
No wonder she's the dart champion. Now, let's go.

00:12:42.804 --> 00:12:44.179
- Come on. -  Great shot!

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:45.430
- Bro. - Let's go.

00:12:45.431 --> 00:12:46.975
I'm not going anywhere.

00:12:47.767 --> 00:12:48.934
Oh!

00:12:48.935 --> 00:12:50.727
The machine was so shocked, it broke.

00:12:51.813 --> 00:12:54.190
Let's go. Come on.

00:12:55.733 --> 00:12:56.817
Bro.

00:12:56.818 --> 00:12:58.152
Learn to accept defeat.

00:12:59.153 --> 00:13:00.154
Come on.

00:13:04.075 --> 00:13:05.076
Let's go.

00:13:11.165 --> 00:13:12.250
Huh?

00:13:12.834 --> 00:13:16.045
Ah, I'm a really great shot, too.

00:13:16.879 --> 00:13:18.631
As great as me?

00:13:42.572 --> 00:13:44.741
Learn to accept the results.

00:13:45.575 --> 00:13:46.742
That's a tiny kitten.

00:14:33.289 --> 00:14:34.290
Just one more round.

00:14:35.333 --> 00:14:36.334
One round.

00:14:50.807 --> 00:14:53.768
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

00:14:58.898 --> 00:14:59.899
Mmm.

00:15:03.111 --> 00:15:04.112
Morning.

00:15:04.821 --> 00:15:06.738
Goodness, look at you.

00:15:07.865 --> 00:15:09.366
What time did you go home?

00:15:09.367 --> 00:15:11.077
Around 3:00 a.m.

00:15:11.953 --> 00:15:14.163
Detective Joo must be really tired, too.

00:15:19.669 --> 00:15:20.752
Good morning.

00:15:20.753 --> 00:15:22.420
Ma'am, are you all right?

00:15:22.421 --> 00:15:23.673
Mmm? What do you mean?

00:15:24.423 --> 00:15:25.924
Let's finish that report today.

00:15:25.925 --> 00:15:27.260
- Yes, ma'am. - Understood.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:35.685
:cue

00:15:36.727 --> 00:15:40.147
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

00:15:45.903 --> 00:15:46.988
AHIN

00:15:55.997 --> 00:15:58.416
AHIN THERE'S A GHOST IN THE ABANDONED HOUSE!

00:15:59.667 --> 00:16:01.877
"Whatever it is, I'll take care of it."

00:16:01.878 --> 00:16:03.211
You startled me.

00:16:03.212 --> 00:16:04.463
DETECTIVE JIN RESPONDING!

00:16:05.464 --> 00:16:07.925
You think you're Batman? Light a signal, why don't you?

00:16:12.054 --> 00:16:15.349
Oh, I do give off that Batman vibe.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:19.353
That's narcissism. It's a disorder, you know.

00:16:19.937 --> 00:16:23.357
You probably don't know, but I'm the cheat code for solving cases.

00:16:24.483 --> 00:16:27.319
You should really see me out there in the field.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.904
I believe I did.

00:16:28.905 --> 00:16:30.364
Frozen, after touching the bomb.

00:16:32.617 --> 00:16:33.743
What's the report about?

00:16:35.828 --> 00:16:37.622
There's a ghost in the abandoned house.

00:16:38.748 --> 00:16:42.000
My name is Park Ahin. I'm a middle school student from Gangha 3-dong.

00:16:42.001 --> 00:16:45.587
My dream is to become a great police officer.

00:16:45.588 --> 00:16:49.050
That's why I have a habit of keeping an eye out for anything suspicious.

00:16:49.717 --> 00:16:51.928
But a few days ago,

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:57.015
I saw these eerie lights floating inside the abandoned house across the street.

00:16:57.016 --> 00:17:00.937
There was a murder there, so the house hasn't sold in years.

00:17:09.362 --> 00:17:11.738
I'm sure it's some kind of vengeful ghost.

00:17:11.739 --> 00:17:14.742
It's asking us to catch the killer.

00:17:16.535 --> 00:17:17.995
How will you take care of this?

00:17:19.163 --> 00:17:20.413
I'll check it out first.

00:17:20.414 --> 00:17:22.667
Mmm. To arrest a ghost?

00:17:23.459 --> 00:17:24.835
Or perform an exorcism?

00:17:26.128 --> 00:17:28.129
What if there's actually something there, huh?

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:29.966
You can't just brush off a tip, damn it.

00:17:30.716 --> 00:17:33.386
By the way, you're straight-up talking down to me now.

00:17:34.011 --> 00:17:35.012
I mean, well,

00:17:36.347 --> 00:17:38.014
We're the same rank now,

00:17:38.015 --> 00:17:39.849
And the same age.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:42.186
And you're not my instructor anymore.

00:17:43.646 --> 00:17:46.482
Do what you want. Who am I to stop a nutjob?

00:17:50.069 --> 00:17:51.653
- Let's head over there. - What?

00:17:51.654 --> 00:17:53.029
Let's go check it out.

00:17:54.907 --> 00:17:56.533
Aren't you clocking out?

00:17:56.534 --> 00:17:57.952
I've got nothing to do at home.

00:17:58.578 --> 00:18:00.120
Forget it. I'm going alone.

00:18:00.121 --> 00:18:01.205
I should come with you.

00:18:02.081 --> 00:18:04.125
What if a ghost latches onto you?

00:18:04.959 --> 00:18:06.377
Come on.

00:18:15.344 --> 00:18:16.429
Let's take your car.

00:18:17.305 --> 00:18:18.723
Why? What is it this time?

00:18:19.307 --> 00:18:21.808
Then we can take my bike and you hang on to my waist.

00:18:21.809 --> 00:18:23.352
No, we can just go separately.

00:18:24.895 --> 00:18:27.314
Come on, don't be so heartless.

00:18:27.315 --> 00:18:29.108
I want to ride in a car like this, too.

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:30.943
Open the door.

00:18:42.163 --> 00:18:43.413
Ooh.

00:18:43.414 --> 00:18:44.749
Nice car.

00:18:48.085 --> 00:18:49.461
Off we go.

00:18:59.096 --> 00:19:00.348
:cue

00:19:13.653 --> 00:19:15.988
FOR SALE

00:19:23.913 --> 00:19:25.039
It's eerie.

00:19:25.539 --> 00:19:27.249
Is this a haunted house or something?

00:19:29.627 --> 00:19:30.710
Oh, my God.

00:19:30.711 --> 00:19:32.837
They actually came.

00:19:32.838 --> 00:19:34.756
Ahin, come out for dinner.

00:19:34.757 --> 00:19:35.758
I'm not eating.

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:55.820
The body was here.

00:19:56.487 --> 00:19:58.197
Do you know what kind of case it was?

00:19:59.281 --> 00:20:00.282
No.

00:20:03.494 --> 00:20:05.329
There was a struggle,

00:20:06.372 --> 00:20:08.290
And they resisted until the end,

00:20:09.166 --> 00:20:12.253
But were eventually killed and became ghosts?

00:20:14.046 --> 00:20:15.423
You believe that?

00:20:16.006 --> 00:20:17.842
- Ghosts and stuff? - No.

00:20:18.926 --> 00:20:20.720
I would if I saw one, but I never have.

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:23.055
I like horror movies, though. You?

00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:25.224
I don't watch that stuff.

00:20:27.184 --> 00:20:28.352
So you get scared easily.

00:20:28.978 --> 00:20:30.478
Of course not.

00:20:30.479 --> 00:20:32.397
I just find them boring, that's all.

00:20:32.398 --> 00:20:33.691
Why bother watching that?

00:20:42.366 --> 00:20:44.659
Oh, come on!

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:46.286
Really boring, isn't it?

00:20:49.999 --> 00:20:51.292
You check upstairs.

00:20:53.169 --> 00:20:54.420
I'll check this side.

00:20:56.464 --> 00:20:58.340
She's seriously annoying.

00:21:21.822 --> 00:21:22.823
Oh!

00:22:20.714 --> 00:22:21.798
Meow.

00:22:23.175 --> 00:22:24.510
:cue

00:22:28.597 --> 00:22:31.057
-  Park Ahin. -  I said I'm not eating.

00:22:31.058 --> 00:22:33.226
Don't you dare make noodles at midnight again.

00:22:33.227 --> 00:22:35.062
Okay, fine. I'm busy.

00:22:35.563 --> 00:22:38.065
- What on earth are you watching with-- - Please just...

00:22:40.526 --> 00:22:42.277
Good luck making it to the academy.

00:22:42.278 --> 00:22:44.654
Just get out.

00:22:44.655 --> 00:22:45.989
Goodness, what are you...

00:22:45.990 --> 00:22:47.074
Park Ahin!

00:23:08.053 --> 00:23:09.263
Detective Jin.

00:23:09.972 --> 00:23:11.222
Jin Isoo!

00:23:11.223 --> 00:23:12.725
Nutjob!

00:23:13.392 --> 00:23:15.144
Yes, ma'am!

00:23:18.022 --> 00:23:19.356
- What's this? - Jin Isoo.

00:23:20.399 --> 00:23:21.400
Snap out of it.

00:23:22.276 --> 00:23:23.818
I'm completely awake.

00:23:23.819 --> 00:23:25.278
What's going on?

00:23:25.279 --> 00:23:27.281
- Hey, what happened? - I don't know.

00:23:27.781 --> 00:23:29.407
I got attacked out of nowhere.

00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:52.055
Hey, try to untie this.

00:23:52.056 --> 00:23:53.348
Okay.

00:23:53.349 --> 00:23:55.225
I actually have pretty long fingers.

00:23:57.394 --> 00:23:58.728
I got it.

00:23:58.729 --> 00:24:00.313
- That's my finger. - Oh.

00:24:00.314 --> 00:24:01.357
Thought it was a rope.

00:24:02.024 --> 00:24:03.900
Stop messing around. We could die here.

00:24:03.901 --> 00:24:05.401
No one's going to die.

00:24:05.402 --> 00:24:06.903
Why are you being so dramatic?

00:24:06.904 --> 00:24:09.113
We don't know who attacked us.

00:24:09.114 --> 00:24:10.823
Okay, fine.

00:24:10.824 --> 00:24:12.076
Just stay still, will you?

00:24:19.833 --> 00:24:20.834
What is it?

00:24:23.253 --> 00:24:24.964
Nothing. It's nothing.

00:24:25.881 --> 00:24:28.132
No need to be alarmed. Stay calm.

00:24:28.133 --> 00:24:29.384
Stay calm.

00:24:29.385 --> 00:24:31.387
Why is this being so difficult?

00:24:35.808 --> 00:24:37.768
Hey, I smell something burning.

00:24:38.352 --> 00:24:39.353
She's got a good nose.

00:24:39.979 --> 00:24:41.980
Is there a fire?

00:24:41.981 --> 00:24:44.650
Kind of. No, it's fine. We're okay for now.

00:24:50.364 --> 00:24:51.447
Hey, Jin Isoo.

00:24:51.448 --> 00:24:53.366
I'm working on it! Jeez.

00:24:53.367 --> 00:24:55.828
Do you see that broken glass over there?

00:24:56.537 --> 00:24:57.912
Yeah.

00:24:57.913 --> 00:24:59.122
On three, fall left.

00:24:59.123 --> 00:25:00.456
Left? Okay.

00:25:00.457 --> 00:25:02.667
One, two,

00:25:02.668 --> 00:25:03.835
Three.

00:25:08.132 --> 00:25:09.383
It was my right.

00:25:10.092 --> 00:25:12.177
You need to be more specific.

00:25:14.096 --> 00:25:15.680
Again. One...

00:25:15.681 --> 00:25:17.224
- Two, three! - Two, three!

00:25:22.688 --> 00:25:23.689
Get up.

00:25:24.314 --> 00:25:26.150
- Get up. - One, two, three.

00:25:28.485 --> 00:25:30.779
Again. One, two, three.

00:25:34.408 --> 00:25:36.160
- Where is it? - Go up.

00:25:37.411 --> 00:25:38.746
A bit farther.

00:25:41.915 --> 00:25:42.916
Got it.

00:25:44.376 --> 00:25:45.710
Be careful.

00:25:45.711 --> 00:25:47.087
Don't move. You'll get hurt.

00:26:10.861 --> 00:26:12.321
Fire.

00:26:13.238 --> 00:26:14.323
It's a fire.

00:26:18.285 --> 00:26:19.952
Yes, this is Violent Crime Team 1.

00:26:19.953 --> 00:26:22.163
There's a fire. :cue

00:26:22.164 --> 00:26:24.541
The detectives went inside, but now it's on fire.

00:26:58.158 --> 00:26:59.243
How do we get out?

00:27:04.748 --> 00:27:06.083
Like this.

00:27:06.708 --> 00:27:07.960
Get out of the way.

00:27:23.100 --> 00:27:24.183
Ladies first.

00:27:33.360 --> 00:27:35.194
If it weren't for me,

00:27:35.195 --> 00:27:37.446
You would've burned to death in that house.

00:27:37.447 --> 00:27:38.907
It would've been the end.

00:27:39.950 --> 00:27:42.535
Detective Joo, just stay close to me from now on.

00:27:42.536 --> 00:27:45.371
The hero never dies that easily.

00:27:45.372 --> 00:27:46.581
You want to live?

00:27:46.582 --> 00:27:49.083
Then just stick close to me, okay?

00:27:49.084 --> 00:27:50.085
Okay.

00:27:52.462 --> 00:27:53.463
What do we do now?

00:27:54.756 --> 00:27:55.924
Do we jump, or not?

00:27:58.051 --> 00:27:59.636
- Like this? - What?

00:28:17.863 --> 00:28:19.363
Nutjob, you okay?

00:28:19.364 --> 00:28:22.075
Yeah. I seriously almost died.

00:28:24.995 --> 00:28:28.122
You should've told me we were jumping. Look how high that is.

00:28:30.584 --> 00:28:32.294
The hero never dies that easily.

00:28:32.961 --> 00:28:34.838
Stay close to me if you want to live.

00:28:44.473 --> 00:28:46.141
There really is something here.

00:28:46.808 --> 00:28:49.353
I have great instincts, huh?

00:28:52.272 --> 00:28:54.274
Oh, you're bleeding.

00:28:55.817 --> 00:28:56.901
I'm fine.

00:28:56.902 --> 00:28:58.654
Come on.

00:28:59.988 --> 00:29:00.989
Give it here.

00:29:06.328 --> 00:29:09.163
- Aah! - You said you were fine.

00:29:09.164 --> 00:29:11.123
You're tying it too tight, so it hurts.

00:29:11.124 --> 00:29:14.085
It's to stop the bleeding.

00:29:14.086 --> 00:29:15.753
You shouldn't have gone overboard.

00:29:15.754 --> 00:29:17.130
That's my thing.

00:29:19.925 --> 00:29:21.176
Jin Isoo!

00:29:24.262 --> 00:29:26.013
- Bro! -  There they are again.

00:29:26.014 --> 00:29:27.223
Are you okay?

00:29:27.224 --> 00:29:28.725
I'm not, but don't make a fuss.

00:29:29.393 --> 00:29:30.686
Are you okay, Detective Joo?

00:29:31.520 --> 00:29:32.895
Yes.

00:29:32.896 --> 00:29:34.438
What happened?

00:29:34.439 --> 00:29:35.440
It was arson.

00:29:35.941 --> 00:29:37.526
Someone tied us up and set a fire.

00:29:45.409 --> 00:29:46.867
Detective!

00:29:47.995 --> 00:29:49.079
Oh.

00:29:53.375 --> 00:29:54.542
Who is this?

00:29:54.543 --> 00:29:58.547
I'm so sorry. I didn't see anything because I was eating noodles.

00:29:59.965 --> 00:30:02.342
Ah, you must be Ahin.

00:30:03.677 --> 00:30:05.929
Are you okay?

00:30:06.513 --> 00:30:07.805
Huh?

00:30:07.806 --> 00:30:10.642
It's nothing. Don't worry about it.

00:30:12.811 --> 00:30:14.937
Have we met somewhere before?

00:30:14.938 --> 00:30:16.523
:cue

00:30:33.623 --> 00:30:36.043
- Take a video of the onlookers. - Yes, ma'am.

00:30:54.436 --> 00:30:57.104
How did you end up here?

00:30:57.105 --> 00:30:58.397
We got a report.

00:30:58.398 --> 00:30:59.857
What kind of report?

00:30:59.858 --> 00:31:03.403
That middle schooler reported that someone keeps entering an empty house.

00:31:04.696 --> 00:31:06.238
We came to check just in case.

00:31:06.239 --> 00:31:07.657
Did you see who attacked you?

00:31:08.992 --> 00:31:10.284
They came up from behind.

00:31:10.285 --> 00:31:12.079
Without knowing who you were?

00:31:12.662 --> 00:31:13.663
Yeah.

00:31:15.457 --> 00:31:17.709
It's not some punk squatting in an empty house.

00:31:19.419 --> 00:31:20.879
There's something going on here.

00:31:52.828 --> 00:31:53.912
What is this?

00:31:56.623 --> 00:31:58.250
Guys, come here. Quickly.

00:32:04.965 --> 00:32:07.174
Let's open it up.

00:32:07.175 --> 00:32:10.011
The padlock is too new for a long-abandoned house.

00:32:10.762 --> 00:32:12.805
Look. Someone tried to pry it open.

00:32:16.893 --> 00:32:17.977
That?

00:32:17.978 --> 00:32:19.729
There's definitely something in there.

00:32:20.397 --> 00:32:21.814
Some kind of dark secret.

00:32:26.444 --> 00:32:28.237
I told you, I've got great instincts.

00:32:28.238 --> 00:32:29.281
You two know that.

00:32:30.365 --> 00:32:31.490
Get a search warrant.

00:32:31.491 --> 00:32:33.701
Why would we need a warrant? We almost died.

00:32:33.702 --> 00:32:34.911
That's not enough.

00:32:39.374 --> 00:32:40.708
We'll say it was on fire.

00:32:40.709 --> 00:32:41.918
We can't.

00:32:42.586 --> 00:32:43.587
Kyungjin.

00:32:46.590 --> 00:32:47.591
We can't.

00:32:53.430 --> 00:32:54.431
Hey, come on.

00:32:55.348 --> 00:32:58.350
If you open it now, whatever we find inside will be inadmissible.

00:32:58.351 --> 00:32:59.352
You know the drill.

00:33:00.187 --> 00:33:01.188
But...

00:33:02.230 --> 00:33:03.939
By the way,

00:33:03.940 --> 00:33:07.319
Why do you keep talking casually to our team leader?

00:33:08.486 --> 00:33:11.364
I told her I'd be respectful, but she kept telling me to relax.

00:33:12.240 --> 00:33:13.365
Goodness.

00:33:13.366 --> 00:33:14.783
She's super chill.

00:33:14.784 --> 00:33:15.952
Honestly.

00:33:17.746 --> 00:33:19.706
Don't open it. Don't you dare.

00:33:38.600 --> 00:33:39.893
Ah...

00:33:46.107 --> 00:33:48.317
Detective Joo, are you okay? Are you hurt?

00:33:48.318 --> 00:33:49.819
No, I'm fine, sir.

00:33:52.530 --> 00:33:53.531
What happened?

00:33:54.866 --> 00:33:56.575
We don't know yet.

00:33:56.576 --> 00:33:59.204
I think we need to do some more digging on this house.

00:33:59.955 --> 00:34:03.582
Okay. I've sent the forensics team, so wrap it up and go home.

00:34:03.583 --> 00:34:04.960
Sir.

00:34:06.628 --> 00:34:08.712
We found a suspicious basement here.

00:34:08.713 --> 00:34:10.382
But it's locked with a padlock.

00:34:11.132 --> 00:34:12.675
Can we get a warrant?

00:34:12.676 --> 00:34:16.011
We need to know what kind of case this is to request a warrant.

00:34:16.012 --> 00:34:18.764
Why? You think it has something to do with the fire?

00:34:18.765 --> 00:34:20.475
I'm not sure.

00:34:21.476 --> 00:34:22.726
In that case,

00:34:22.727 --> 00:34:25.188
Investigate first, then get a warrant if you need to.

00:34:26.064 --> 00:34:27.607
Yes, sir.

00:34:32.654 --> 00:34:35.240
- We'll have to see about the warrant. - Okay.

00:34:40.120 --> 00:34:42.413
The fire started on the first floor,

00:34:42.414 --> 00:34:45.165
Then appears to have spread up the stairs.

00:34:45.166 --> 00:34:47.543
I heard there was a murder here a long time ago,

00:34:47.544 --> 00:34:49.837
But someone's been in and out since then.

00:34:49.838 --> 00:34:52.132
Okay. We'll look for any recent traces.

00:34:54.301 --> 00:34:57.177
We'll go collect security footage from the streets nearby.

00:34:57.178 --> 00:34:58.262
Okay.

00:34:58.263 --> 00:34:59.805
- Let's go. - Okay.

00:35:10.525 --> 00:35:11.526
-  Jin Isoo! -  Hey! :cue

00:35:14.029 --> 00:35:15.988
- What are you doing? - I told you not to.

00:35:18.742 --> 00:35:19.784
Hey!

00:35:20.827 --> 00:35:24.581
Is it illegal for a homeowner to break down his own door?

00:35:25.081 --> 00:35:26.082
No way.

00:35:26.958 --> 00:35:28.292
I bought this house.

00:35:28.293 --> 00:35:30.419
You bought it?

00:35:30.420 --> 00:35:32.671
The realtor's number was on the front gate.

00:35:32.672 --> 00:35:33.797
FOR SALE

00:35:35.216 --> 00:35:37.509
The owner asked them to sell it no matter what.

00:35:37.510 --> 00:35:40.095
So you just bought it?

00:35:40.096 --> 00:35:41.180
Wow, bro.

00:35:42.432 --> 00:35:44.100
Who just spends money like that...

00:35:45.435 --> 00:35:47.686
Except you, of course.

00:35:47.687 --> 00:35:48.771
You know how to flex.

00:35:48.772 --> 00:35:49.897
Mmm.

00:35:49.898 --> 00:35:52.274
So this is your cheat code.

00:35:52.275 --> 00:35:54.777
This is nothing to be surprised about.

00:35:54.778 --> 00:35:56.071
You're pretty timid.

00:35:57.364 --> 00:35:59.073
Where did you get that hammer?

00:35:59.074 --> 00:36:01.784
I borrowed it from Ahin. They're repairing their wall.

00:36:01.785 --> 00:36:03.536
All right, then.

00:36:05.747 --> 00:36:08.333
Now, don't be shy.

00:36:08.917 --> 00:36:10.668
Welcome.

00:36:47.580 --> 00:36:48.581
Detective Joo.

00:36:49.958 --> 00:36:51.126
That looks newly covered.

00:37:03.138 --> 00:37:04.139
Kyungjin.

00:37:15.775 --> 00:37:16.776
Stand back.

00:37:36.546 --> 00:37:37.547
Detective Joo.

00:38:47.450 --> 00:38:49.285
GANGHA 3-DONG BURIED BODIES CASE

00:38:52.288 --> 00:38:55.083
How did you end up going to that house?

00:38:55.583 --> 00:38:57.502
We received a tip.

00:38:59.254 --> 00:39:00.505
What kind of tip?

00:39:01.965 --> 00:39:04.008
Someone reported that there was a ghost.

00:39:04.634 --> 00:39:05.759
To me.

00:39:09.097 --> 00:39:11.849
Hey, what is he talking about? Did he just say a ghost?

00:39:11.850 --> 00:39:14.811
It was a report of lights in an empty house.

00:39:15.353 --> 00:39:18.648
We went to check if it was being used for criminal activity.

00:39:19.440 --> 00:39:20.441
Okay, fine.

00:39:21.442 --> 00:39:23.652
Why did you open the basement? I said wait.

00:39:23.653 --> 00:39:25.488
I went ahead and bought the house!

00:39:28.616 --> 00:39:29.617
I see.

00:39:30.285 --> 00:39:31.411
You bought the house.

00:39:37.834 --> 00:39:38.959
Right, so,

00:39:38.960 --> 00:39:41.753
You uncovered five bodies?

00:39:41.754 --> 00:39:43.881
Yes, they're performing the autopsy now.

00:39:43.882 --> 00:39:45.257
ONE BODY, BURIED RECENTLY

00:39:45.258 --> 00:39:48.552
Four of them are skeletal remains, so identifying them will take a while.

00:39:50.221 --> 00:39:51.722
For now,

00:39:51.723 --> 00:39:53.640
Team 1 and 2 will both be on this case.

00:39:53.641 --> 00:39:55.767
Make sure this doesn't leak to the press,

00:39:55.768 --> 00:39:58.020
And identify the victims quickly. Got it?

00:39:58.021 --> 00:39:59.439
- Yes, sir. -  Yes, sir.

00:40:00.899 --> 00:40:02.984
:cue

00:40:15.413 --> 00:40:17.582
Let's begin the autopsy.

00:41:01.000 --> 00:41:03.628
I investigated the murder that happened inside the house.

00:41:04.629 --> 00:41:07.923
Around 1:00 a.m. on October 25, 2016,

00:41:07.924 --> 00:41:11.469
A couple and their son, a college student, were all murdered.

00:41:13.596 --> 00:41:15.640
There were no signs of forced entry,

00:41:16.307 --> 00:41:18.016
But cash and jewelry were gone,

00:41:18.017 --> 00:41:20.645
So it was suspected to be a robbery-homicide,

00:41:21.187 --> 00:41:22.813
But the culprit was never caught.

00:41:22.814 --> 00:41:24.273
It's a cold case.

00:41:25.233 --> 00:41:26.900
No fingerprints, no hair.

00:41:26.901 --> 00:41:28.902
Not a single trace was left behind.

00:41:28.903 --> 00:41:32.907
So the house was abandoned after that, and then it was used as a burial site.

00:41:33.700 --> 00:41:35.201
By the serial killer.

00:41:39.789 --> 00:41:40.790
Detective Joo.

00:41:42.375 --> 00:41:44.960
The most recently deceased victim

00:41:44.961 --> 00:41:46.462
Had these glasses in their pants.

00:41:49.799 --> 00:41:51.634
I'll go check it out.

00:41:52.218 --> 00:41:53.969
Okay. We'll go after the arsonist.

00:41:53.970 --> 00:41:55.387
Got it. Let's go.

00:41:55.388 --> 00:41:56.389
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

00:41:58.141 --> 00:42:00.977
- Let's check the footage from the scene. - Okay.

00:42:14.240 --> 00:42:15.533
Stop.

00:42:16.826 --> 00:42:18.869
That's the guy. The black hoodie.

00:42:18.870 --> 00:42:20.454
- Track him. - Okay.

00:42:40.141 --> 00:42:41.266
It's a rental.

00:42:41.267 --> 00:42:42.643
- Run the plate. - Got it.

00:42:49.817 --> 00:42:50.818
Excuse me.

00:42:52.445 --> 00:42:53.528
We're with the police.

00:42:53.529 --> 00:42:54.696
How can I help you?

00:42:54.697 --> 00:42:56.448
Could you tell us

00:42:56.449 --> 00:42:59.409
Where you supplied these glasses?

00:42:59.410 --> 00:43:00.953
I'll check right away.

00:43:06.918 --> 00:43:07.919
DOHYUN CAR RENTAL

00:43:10.171 --> 00:43:12.006
Who rented this car?

00:43:12.840 --> 00:43:15.259
Oh, that car hasn't been returned yet.

00:43:15.718 --> 00:43:16.719
One moment, please.

00:43:23.017 --> 00:43:24.018
Oh...

00:43:25.645 --> 00:43:26.646
It's that car there.

00:43:28.981 --> 00:43:29.982
Right.

00:43:32.902 --> 00:43:34.112
Hey, hey.

00:43:40.118 --> 00:43:41.201
Police.

00:43:41.202 --> 00:43:43.662
Please come out, serial killer.

00:43:43.663 --> 00:43:45.038
Careful. He could be armed.

00:43:45.039 --> 00:43:46.290
You're right.

00:43:48.751 --> 00:43:49.960
Come out.

00:43:49.961 --> 00:43:51.170
Or we'll break it.

00:44:15.069 --> 00:44:18.114
JEONG DAEUN GANGHA 3-DONG ARSON SUSPECT

00:44:25.121 --> 00:44:26.747
Inside that abandoned house,

00:44:28.457 --> 00:44:29.500
Did you attack us?

00:44:30.084 --> 00:44:31.293
What?

00:44:31.294 --> 00:44:33.545
Did you knock us out and tie us up?

00:44:33.546 --> 00:44:36.423
No, how would I even do that?

00:44:36.424 --> 00:44:39.134
Last night, you were at the abandoned house

00:44:39.135 --> 00:44:40.469
At 14-1 Gangha 3-dong, right?

00:44:41.846 --> 00:44:42.847
Yes.

00:44:45.141 --> 00:44:47.642
I started the fire.

00:44:49.020 --> 00:44:50.687
We almost burned to death.

00:44:50.688 --> 00:44:52.522
My team leader hurt her arm. :cue

00:44:52.523 --> 00:44:55.610
I'm really sorry. I didn't know there were people inside.

00:44:56.944 --> 00:44:58.529
Why did you start the fire?

00:44:59.572 --> 00:45:01.616
Because Hyeonsu disappeared,

00:45:03.201 --> 00:45:05.328
And no one will believe me.

00:45:07.038 --> 00:45:08.789
Please start from the beginning.

00:45:10.499 --> 00:45:13.084
Hyeonsu is a lawyer.

00:45:14.629 --> 00:45:16.297
We've been dating for three years,

00:45:17.465 --> 00:45:19.342
And we were about to get married.

00:45:22.053 --> 00:45:23.178
4 MONTHS AGO

00:45:24.722 --> 00:45:27.057
JEONG DAEUN'S FIANCÉ PARK HYEONSU

00:45:29.644 --> 00:45:31.311
-  It's raining. - Hold on.

00:45:31.312 --> 00:45:32.896
- What? - It's raining so suddenly.

00:45:32.897 --> 00:45:34.941
Let's go.

00:45:37.401 --> 00:45:39.528
He was a really kind person.

00:45:42.990 --> 00:45:45.492
When we were busy planning our wedding,

00:45:45.493 --> 00:45:47.578
He said something important had come up.

00:45:48.204 --> 00:45:50.915
His former classmate was in trouble and needed his help.

00:45:51.540 --> 00:45:53.834
Not long after, she was murdered.

00:45:54.543 --> 00:45:55.920
But then I was told

00:45:56.462 --> 00:45:58.421
That Hyeonsu was the killer.

00:45:58.422 --> 00:46:00.966
I kept saying he'd never do something like that,

00:46:00.967 --> 00:46:02.551
But no one would believe me.

00:46:04.095 --> 00:46:05.887
They said all the evidence was there,

00:46:05.888 --> 00:46:08.724
That she and Hyeonsu used to date,

00:46:09.267 --> 00:46:12.144
That he stalked her to get back with her, then killed her.

00:46:12.895 --> 00:46:14.480
But that doesn't make any sense.

00:46:16.315 --> 00:46:17.399
Sir.

00:46:18.693 --> 00:46:19.694
What is it?

00:46:27.368 --> 00:46:29.287
PARK HYEONSU

00:46:38.754 --> 00:46:40.506
Then why did you go to that house?

00:46:47.930 --> 00:46:51.433
Hyeonsu installed a location-sharing app on my phone.

00:46:53.644 --> 00:46:56.188
This app will show you where I am.

00:46:59.734 --> 00:47:01.360
We can't see each other very often.

00:47:02.111 --> 00:47:05.740
Now, if you just check the app, you'll know where I'm working.

00:47:06.449 --> 00:47:07.824
Oh, you.

00:47:09.952 --> 00:47:11.369
On the day of the murder,

00:47:11.370 --> 00:47:14.914
Hyeonsu's last location was that house.

00:47:14.915 --> 00:47:18.377
At first, I was too shaken and forgot all about the app.

00:47:19.045 --> 00:47:21.463
When I later checked and went to his last location,

00:47:21.464 --> 00:47:22.590
It was an abandoned house.

00:47:23.382 --> 00:47:25.926
Hyeonsu has no connection to that neighborhood.

00:47:27.386 --> 00:47:28.387
Wait, so,

00:47:29.180 --> 00:47:30.806
You went in there alone?

00:47:32.224 --> 00:47:33.308
Weren't you scared?

00:47:33.309 --> 00:47:35.268
I asked the police to investigate,

00:47:35.269 --> 00:47:37.855
But the detective in charge wouldn't listen.

00:47:43.652 --> 00:47:46.864
But there was a strange basement there.

00:47:51.369 --> 00:47:52.953
I tried to open it...

00:48:01.003 --> 00:48:02.296
...but I couldn't.

00:48:03.130 --> 00:48:04.382
So I set the place on fire,

00:48:06.217 --> 00:48:08.886
Thinking they might find something while putting it out.

00:48:10.262 --> 00:48:12.681
I honestly didn't know someone was inside.

00:48:14.308 --> 00:48:15.434
By any chance,

00:48:16.268 --> 00:48:18.020
Did you see anyone suspicious there?

00:48:19.355 --> 00:48:21.482
No, no one.

00:48:38.874 --> 00:48:39.958
Jiwon.

00:48:41.502 --> 00:48:42.586
Hi.

00:48:43.337 --> 00:48:45.464
Have you eaten at all?

00:48:46.173 --> 00:48:47.382
No.

00:48:47.383 --> 00:48:48.926
I wasn't really hungry.

00:48:50.344 --> 00:48:51.429
I got you a sandwich.

00:48:52.638 --> 00:48:53.639
Thanks.

00:48:55.516 --> 00:48:56.725
I'll eat it later.

00:49:01.313 --> 00:49:03.441
Did you find anything?

00:49:06.318 --> 00:49:08.946
We start work on the skeletal remains tomorrow morning.

00:49:09.530 --> 00:49:12.365
We performed the autopsy on the most recent victim first...

00:49:15.953 --> 00:49:18.581
...but the body's too decomposed to recover any fingerprints.

00:49:19.331 --> 00:49:22.042
Look here. There are three stab wounds.

00:49:22.626 --> 00:49:26.171
And the wrists have marks that appear to be from duct tape.

00:49:26.172 --> 00:49:29.008
So the victim was stabbed while tied up?

00:49:31.927 --> 00:49:32.928
Yes. :cue

00:49:38.267 --> 00:49:41.019
DETECTIVE DIVISION

00:49:41.020 --> 00:49:42.104
You? Against me?

00:49:42.605 --> 00:49:44.355
That's ridiculous.

00:49:44.356 --> 00:49:45.357
It's him.

00:49:47.318 --> 00:49:49.403
The detective who wouldn't believe me.

00:49:58.204 --> 00:50:00.122
Sir, how did this happen?

00:50:02.666 --> 00:50:05.002
We didn't make a mistake.

00:50:20.768 --> 00:50:21.810
INVESTIGATION REPORT

00:50:22.937 --> 00:50:24.730
Three months ago, in Yuseon-dong,

00:50:25.481 --> 00:50:27.023
Kim Minseo was murdered.

00:50:30.069 --> 00:50:31.445
- Hello. - Hello.

00:50:41.539 --> 00:50:43.164
The suspect fled on a motorcycle,

00:50:43.165 --> 00:50:45.251
Entered Park Hyeonsu's house...

00:50:51.048 --> 00:50:53.175
...then drove away in his car.

00:50:59.473 --> 00:51:00.849
Even so,

00:51:01.976 --> 00:51:03.685
Would a man about to get married,

00:51:03.686 --> 00:51:06.188
Who was sharing his location with his girlfriend,

00:51:07.064 --> 00:51:08.774
Plan and execute a murder?

00:51:09.608 --> 00:51:10.734
It doesn't make sense.

00:51:14.446 --> 00:51:15.447
What was his motive?

00:51:20.077 --> 00:51:22.413
Park Hyeonsu kept texting her, asking to meet up.

00:51:23.581 --> 00:51:25.081
Did you take care of it?

00:51:25.082 --> 00:51:27.209
I'll be waiting, so tell me when you're done.

00:51:28.335 --> 00:51:30.420
If you keep this up, I'm not holding back.

00:51:30.421 --> 00:51:31.713
Please meet me just once.

00:51:31.714 --> 00:51:33.006
You want to see me lose it?

00:51:33.007 --> 00:51:34.800
Kim Minseo kept refusing.

00:51:35.384 --> 00:51:36.760
Kim Minseo

00:51:37.595 --> 00:51:39.929
Had filed a stalking complaint before.

00:51:39.930 --> 00:51:42.766
Park Hyeonsu's fingerprints were on a knife found at the scene.

00:51:45.102 --> 00:51:48.271
That knife was the knife missing from Park Hyeonsu's house.

00:51:48.272 --> 00:51:51.859
We also found the disguise he used as a courier inside his house.

00:51:52.860 --> 00:51:55.695
We confirmed the weapon, fingerprints, motive, and movements.

00:51:55.696 --> 00:51:58.449
Then he suddenly disappeared, so we put him on the wanted list.

00:52:00.326 --> 00:52:01.327
But...

00:52:07.041 --> 00:52:08.751
These belong to Park Hyeonsu.

00:52:16.091 --> 00:52:17.217
Got the autopsy results?

00:52:18.594 --> 00:52:21.971
They'll do the rest tomorrow, so this is just the most recent victim's.

00:52:21.972 --> 00:52:25.933
A male in his 30s. Died three months ago, and stabbed to death while bound.

00:52:39.239 --> 00:52:41.158
Wait, so,

00:52:41.992 --> 00:52:45.161
The murder suspect you were after three months ago

00:52:45.162 --> 00:52:48.082
Was murdered and his body was found at the abandoned house?

00:52:50.834 --> 00:52:54.296
Did someone get revenge on him?

00:52:55.214 --> 00:52:56.799
Does Kim Minseo have any family?

00:52:57.841 --> 00:52:59.509
Her husband and her parents.

00:52:59.510 --> 00:53:02.638
How can you find and kill someone even the police couldn't find?

00:53:03.472 --> 00:53:05.891
What about the abandoned house? Did he even go there?

00:53:06.600 --> 00:53:09.727
His phone went offline near there and never came back online.

00:53:09.728 --> 00:53:13.065
His car was found abandoned at Incheon Port.

00:53:13.565 --> 00:53:17.151
We assumed he'd snuck out of the country by sea,

00:53:17.152 --> 00:53:19.780
So we had Interpol issue a Red Notice.

00:53:30.124 --> 00:53:31.750
Let's verify this first. :cue

00:53:32.668 --> 00:53:36.295
Ask them to compare the body's DNA with Park Hyeonsu's.

00:53:36.296 --> 00:53:37.297
Yes, ma'am.

00:53:44.012 --> 00:53:45.013
Yes, sir.

00:53:46.056 --> 00:53:47.307
Yes, understood.

00:54:01.405 --> 00:54:02.406
Yes, come in.

00:54:04.032 --> 00:54:05.450
Detective Joo, have a seat.

00:54:06.702 --> 00:54:09.288
I'm going fishing at dawn.

00:54:09.955 --> 00:54:12.541
If I catch some big ones, would you like one?

00:54:13.250 --> 00:54:16.586
They don't call me the Sea King's eldest son for nothing.

00:54:16.587 --> 00:54:17.796
I'm all right, thank you.

00:54:19.965 --> 00:54:21.175
So,

00:54:22.468 --> 00:54:25.052
I hear Jin Isoo bought a house.

00:54:25.053 --> 00:54:26.345
Yes, sir.

00:54:26.346 --> 00:54:29.725
And you found five bodies inside?

00:54:30.309 --> 00:54:31.518
Yes, sir.

00:54:32.269 --> 00:54:34.980
Does he just make trouble wherever he goes?

00:54:37.649 --> 00:54:39.650
- Is there nothing wrong with that? - Pardon?

00:54:39.651 --> 00:54:43.280
I mean, is there anything we can find fault with?

00:54:44.364 --> 00:54:47.784
Can a police officer just buy up a house like that?

00:54:48.494 --> 00:54:49.786
There's no reason he can't.

00:54:50.871 --> 00:54:52.372
He's not breaking the law.

00:54:53.040 --> 00:54:54.957
We found five bodies there

00:54:54.958 --> 00:54:57.752
And prevented it from becoming the perfect crime,

00:54:57.753 --> 00:54:58.878
So it's a good thing.

00:54:58.879 --> 00:55:00.631
How is that a good thing?

00:55:01.215 --> 00:55:02.298
Come on,

00:55:02.299 --> 00:55:05.719
I just want to make it to retirement in peace, for God's sake.

00:55:10.140 --> 00:55:12.267
Should we hand this over to Seoul Headquarters?

00:55:13.101 --> 00:55:14.895
It's a big case.

00:55:16.730 --> 00:55:19.525
Don't worry, sir. We'll catch whoever's behind this.

00:55:24.112 --> 00:55:25.155
NO USABLE FINGERPRINTS

00:55:26.323 --> 00:55:28.324
SUSPECT, VICTIM

00:55:28.325 --> 00:55:30.786
PARK HYEONSU, AGE 34 KIM MINSEO, AGE 34

00:55:32.037 --> 00:55:33.704
VICTIM KIM MINSEO'S HOUSE

00:55:33.705 --> 00:55:34.957
SUSPECT PARK HYEONSU'S HOUSE

00:55:38.252 --> 00:55:40.002
Ma'am, we got a match on the DNA.

00:55:40.003 --> 00:55:41.046
It is Park Hyeonsu.

00:55:42.673 --> 00:55:43.674
AUTOPSY REPORT

00:55:45.592 --> 00:55:48.387
Who could have killed Park Hyeonsu?

00:55:50.847 --> 00:55:52.266
Don't just think about him.

00:55:53.267 --> 00:55:55.310
There are five bodies killed by the same guy.

00:55:59.231 --> 00:56:00.566
Then, was Park Hyeonsu

00:56:01.775 --> 00:56:03.652
Murdered by a serial killer?

00:56:04.611 --> 00:56:05.612
No, wait.

00:56:07.114 --> 00:56:08.156
Let's start over.

00:56:15.414 --> 00:56:18.041
What if Park Hyeonsu wasn't the one who killed Kim Minseo?

00:56:18.917 --> 00:56:20.502
You're saying they're professionals?

00:56:21.837 --> 00:56:22.838
Yes.

00:56:25.465 --> 00:56:29.344
If Park Hyeonsu wasn't the one who killed Kim Minseo...

00:56:32.889 --> 00:56:34.599
It's the perfect crime.

00:56:34.600 --> 00:56:35.726
Right? Here, look.

00:56:36.393 --> 00:56:38.644
Look. The target.

00:56:38.645 --> 00:56:41.063
A victim to frame as the suspect.

00:56:41.064 --> 00:56:43.482
If they kill the target and the suspect,

00:56:43.483 --> 00:56:45.193
Then make him go missing,

00:56:45.777 --> 00:56:47.529
The case cannot be solved.

00:56:48.989 --> 00:56:50.782
Five perfect crimes.

00:56:51.491 --> 00:56:54.161
You need at least two people to make this possible.

00:56:54.828 --> 00:56:56.579
They're methodical and cold.

00:56:56.580 --> 00:56:58.248
Park Hyeonsu would've been first,

00:56:58.874 --> 00:57:00.167
Since they sent those texts.

00:57:02.753 --> 00:57:04.921
First, they overpowered Park Hyeonsu.

00:57:07.424 --> 00:57:09.134
One of them would've kept watch.

00:57:14.723 --> 00:57:16.642
They sent the harassing messages.

00:57:17.267 --> 00:57:18.768
- Hello. - Hello, delivery.

00:57:18.769 --> 00:57:20.519
Then, after killing the target...

00:57:23.106 --> 00:57:24.691
...they dressed up as Park Hyeonsu. :cue

00:57:45.545 --> 00:57:47.214
Help me!

00:57:59.893 --> 00:58:01.686
Then they buried him and disappeared.

00:58:01.687 --> 00:58:03.355
So they're professional killers?

00:58:04.189 --> 00:58:05.190
Yes.

00:58:05.857 --> 00:58:07.775
They must've been hired to do it.

00:58:09.444 --> 00:58:12.405
Those bastards completely fooled me.

00:58:12.406 --> 00:58:14.157
We need to start this case over.

00:58:15.117 --> 00:58:18.120
The ones who attacked you and Isoo must be the real culprits.

00:58:19.454 --> 00:58:21.330
If they came to the house...

00:58:21.331 --> 00:58:23.208
It means they killed someone else.

00:58:24.251 --> 00:58:25.836
They were there to bury the body.

00:58:34.594 --> 00:58:35.595
Wait.

00:58:37.097 --> 00:58:39.015
It's blood.

00:58:39.474 --> 00:58:40.558
KILLER 1 JANG JAECHUN

00:58:40.559 --> 00:58:41.642
It leaked.

00:58:41.643 --> 00:58:42.727
KILLER 2 JO BEOMKI

00:58:42.728 --> 00:58:43.811
What do we do?

00:58:45.439 --> 00:58:46.857
This is bad.

00:58:48.567 --> 00:58:49.693
Taegwang.

00:59:07.794 --> 00:59:08.961
FLEX X COP 2 EPISODE 3

00:59:08.962 --> 00:59:10.296
THE KILLER OF KILLERS YU TAEGWANG

00:59:34.821 --> 00:59:38.241
Special Cast. Lee Hakju, Park Soi

00:59:45.332 --> 00:59:46.874
We got a new job. Where are you?

00:59:46.875 --> 00:59:48.293
I got their location.

00:59:48.543 --> 00:59:49.627
I need the chopper.

00:59:49.628 --> 00:59:51.253
This is straight out of a soap opera.

00:59:51.254 --> 00:59:52.546
You're Korean, right?

00:59:52.547 --> 00:59:54.090
- I don't know. - You don't know?

00:59:54.883 --> 00:59:56.801
- Freeze. - We're flying out at dawn.

00:59:56.802 --> 00:59:59.470
They're ruthless killers, so civilians could get hurt.

00:59:59.471 --> 01:00:00.472
Beomki!

01:00:01.056 --> 01:00:02.139
If we want to catch them...

01:00:02.140 --> 01:00:03.391
Let's hire them to kill someone.

01:00:03.767 --> 01:00:05.894
Is this how you normally investigate?

01:00:07.103 --> 01:00:09.063
I won't let you down.

01:00:09.064 --> 01:00:10.648
You were a real scumbag.

01:00:10.649 --> 01:00:12.024
We all go down together.

01:00:12.025 --> 01:00:13.318
So the perp's still here.

01:00:16.363 --> 01:00:17.739
Jin Isoo!

01:00:41.555 --> 01:00:44.056
Who is that?

01:00:44.057 --> 01:00:45.851
Did we arrest a gang boss?

01:00:47.519 --> 01:00:49.144
Is that Park?

01:00:50.272 --> 01:00:51.273
Gosh.

01:00:52.983 --> 01:00:54.608
What are they doing?

01:00:54.609 --> 01:00:56.695
I have no idea, sir.

01:01:07.289 --> 01:01:08.789
Our district

01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:10.876
Is just strange overall.

01:01:11.585 --> 01:01:13.587
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

